\(v_{4}\) of particle \(i\) at a certain \(p_{t}\) can be obtained by three-particle (\(i\), \(j\), \(k\)) correlations:

\[\langle\cos(4\phi_{i}-2\phi_{j}-2\phi_{k})\rangle=v_{4}(p_{t})v_{2}^{2}, \tag{4.2}\]

where the average is taken over all the particles and events. The dominant non-flow contribution to the three particle correlation can be estimated as follows: if particle \(i\) is correlated with particle \(j\) by non-flow and correlated with particle \(k\) by flow, the three-particle non-flow correlations can be written like:

\[g_{2}\times\langle\cos(2\phi_{i}-2\phi_{k})\rangle=g_{2}\times v_{2}\{4\}(p_{t })v_{2} \tag{4.3}\]

where \(g_{2}\) is the non-flow contribution from two-particle correlations. It is shown that \(g_{2}\propto v_{2}^{2}\{2\}(p_{t})-v_{2}^{2}\{4\}(p_{t})\)[49, 95]. Therefore, the non-flow contributions to \(v_{4}(p_{t})\) is obtained by:

\[\frac{g_{2}\times v_{2}\{4\}(p_{t})v_{2}}{v_{2}^{2}}=\frac{(v_{2}^{2}\{2\}(p_ {t})-v_{2}^{2}\{4\}(p_{t}))\times v_{2}\{4\}(p_{t})}{v_{2}}. \tag{4.4}\]

The non-flow contributions to \(v_{4}/v_{2}^{2}\) is then estimated by

\[\frac{v_{2}^{2}\{2\}(p_{t})-v_{2}^{2}\{4\}(p_{t})}{v_{2}v_{2}\{4\}(p_{t})}. \tag{4.5}\]

The brackets in this figure show the lower limit of the ratio due to these systematic uncertainties. However, if the complete difference in \(v_{2}^{2}\{2\}-v_{2}^{2}\{4\}\) originates from flow fluctuations, the systematic error will be reduced.

